ured Confedera","","","n9709342307"],["Columbiad","plaque","This replica of a coast defense cannon known as the columbiad was manufactured, 1964, by Savannah Machine and Foundry Company as a public service. A similar cannon was positioned here during Union naval attacks, 1863. The columbiad fired 87 lb. shells. It","","","n9709342304"],["Capt. Nicholas Clinch","plaque","When called upon by a Union officer to surrender during Sherman's assault, December 13, 1864, Clinch responded with a blow of his sword. After three sabre, six bayonet, and two gunshot wounds, he was taken.","","","n9709342306"],["Fort McAllister / The Naval Bombardments","plaque","Please see photo https://www.mapillary.com/app/?pKey=787452075620799&focus=photo&lat=31.891616100003&lng=-81.195563&z=17","","","n9709342309"],["Major Gallie's Gun","plaque","In this emplacement, chosen nearest the enemy, was the gun, an 8-inch columbiad, commanded personally by Major John B. Gallie.","","","n9709342303"],["Fort McAllister / The Assault from the Rear","plaque","Please see photo https://www.mapillary.com/app/?pKey=714447259798590&focus=photo&lat=31.8901985&lng=-81.194930900002&z=17","","","n9709342308"],["Pin Point Community","plaque","","","","n11244970256"],["Sandfly Historic Marker","plaque","","","","n8361371217"],["Native American Area","archaeological_site","","","","w1236161890"],["Isle of Hope Historical Marker","history board","","","","n8383804816"],["Sgt. Ebbie Paxton Monument","monument","marble column","","","n9218088252"],["Jim Richmond donation of property to Garden Club","plaque","","","","n11909629885"],["Nickie's Fountain","plaque","","","","n9607658710"],["End of U.S. 80 Tybee Island Korean War Veterans Memorial Highway","memorial","End of U.S. 80 Tybee Island Korean War Veterans Memorial Highway Dedicated 4/7/08 by the Republic of Korea and a grateful nation","2008-04-07","","n9607814595"],["South Fort","fort","","","","n12603839002"],["Historical plaque","plaque","","","","n12603802522"